Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/31] devtools: give a page an untrusted debugging session

An application that wants to read a page's network, or run the
protocol against one page, has the remote debugging server, which
serves every page of every profile to whatever connects to its port.
There is no way to speak the protocol to one page alone.

QWebEngineDevToolsSession attaches to a page by its devToolsId, which
QWebEnginePage and WebEngineView already report, and carries protocol
JSON both ways through sendMessage and messageReceived. Its
DevToolsAgentHostClient is not trusted, so Chromium answers
Target.getTargets, Target.attachToTarget and attachToBrowserTarget with
an error: the session reaches the page and the children
Target.setAutoAttach brings, such as a cross-site frame, and no other
page, worker or the browser. It may not read or write local files and
is refused the operations kept for privileged automation clients. An id
that is not a page's own, such as a worker's, is refused at attach.

The session ends on detach, when the page closes and when it is
destroyed, and says so with detached and attachedChanged.

omaweb#373

